 "summary": "URL-embedded query language of the Open Data Protocol: system query options ($filter, $select, $expand, $orderby, $top/$skip, $count, $search, $compute, $apply) with a common expression syntax of operators, canonical functions and lambda operators over an entity data model.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "international-standard",
  "consortium-standard"
 ],
 "standards": [
  "OASIS OData Version 4.01",
  "ISO/IEC 20802-1:2016"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://www.odata.org/",
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "OData 4.01 Part 2: URL Conventions defines the query syntax normatively, with an ABNF in the separate 'ABNF Construction Rules'. Aggregation ($apply) is defined by the Data Aggregation Extension. OData 4.0 is also ISO/IEC 20802.",
  "0": "Apache Olingo (Java) and Microsoft's odata.net (C#) are the main open-source server/client libraries."
 },
